# .dockerignore — the build context for EVERY image in this repo.
#
# One file, deliberately, and not a per-Dockerfile `Dockerfile.api.dockerignore`
# set: a Dockerfile-specific ignore file takes PRECEDENCE over this one rather
# than merging with it, so each would have to restate every rule below and a new
# exclusion added here would silently not apply to those builds.
#
# Two of the rules are load-bearing rather than hygiene — an unreadable path
# fails the build outright, and `Dockerfile.base` ends in `COPY . /app`, so
# anything not excluded here lands in the base image that api and mcp build
# FROM. Both are called out where they appear.
#
# Almost everything here is gitignored too, so CI builds from a clean checkout
# never see it and only local builds do. That asymmetry is exactly why the rules
# have to be written down rather than assumed.

# ── Virtual environments & caches ──────────────────────────────
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# ── Git ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# ── Paths that BREAK the build, not just bloat it ─────────────
# Git worktrees checked out under the repo, and the redroid emulator's state
# dirs. Both hold root-owned files the emulator created (an adb socket) that the
# context sender cannot read, so the build fails with EACCES while transferring
# the context — before any COPY runs, and with an error that names the file
# rather than the reason. Never build inputs in any case.
.worktrees/
apps/mewbo_aura/tools/redroid/data/
apps/mewbo_aura/tools/redroid/data-gms/

# ── Generated build output — the bulk of the context ──────────
# The Android Gradle output alone was ~1.6 GB of a ~3.4 GB context, re-sent on
# every build of every image, and no image copies any of it: the Aura client is
# built on the host and in CI, never inside these containers. The app SOURCE
# stays available; only what Gradle regenerates is dropped.
apps/mewbo_aura/app/build/
apps/mewbo_aura/build/
**/.gradle/
**/.cxx/
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
# mkdocs render output and the interview-docs scratch tree — both regenerated,
# together another ~120 MB.
site/
docs-interview/

# ── Node / frontend build artifacts ──────────────────────────
**/node_modules/
apps/mewbo_console/dist/
apps/mewbo_ide/dist/

# ── Environment & secrets ─────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
docker.env
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.pem
**/*.p12

# ── Runtime init scripts — never baked into ANY image ─────────
# docker/init.d/*.sh is bind-mounted read-only by docker-compose.yml and sourced
# by docker/entrypoint.sh at start, so runtime setup can be edited, or a tool
# version pinned, with a restart instead of a rebuild.
#
# Excluding it HERE is what makes that true — dropping the COPY lines was not
# enough, because `COPY . /app` in Dockerfile.base swept the directory into the
# base image and the scripts kept arriving with no COPY naming them.
#
# It also closes a leak a hand-maintained allowlist used to guard: this
# directory is gitignored apart from the tracked few, so a build from a dirty
# tree would bake a developer's local-only script — one naming an internal
# host — into a published image. Now neither build can, and there is no
# allowlist left to forget to update.
docker/init.d/

# ── Operator config — never baked into ANY image ──────────────
# Same contract as docker/init.d/ above: an operator's app.json / mcp.json is
# runtime identity, not build capability. Both are gitignored, and both the api
# and mewbo-mcp services bind-mount ./configs over /app/configs, so a baked copy
# is shadowed the instant a container starts and only ever serves to leak.
#
# It is also load-bearing for the BUILD. Operator config carries `${VAR}`
# references whose values arrive at runtime through env_file, and the config
# validator refuses an unresolved reference. Any build step that imports mewbo
# code resolves config transitively — a logger call alone reaches
# get_config_value — so a baked app.json turns "the gateway URL lives in the
# environment" into a build that cannot complete. The tracked *.example.json
# files stay: they hold literals, and they are the fallback a fresh checkout
# builds against.
configs/app.json
configs/mcp.json

# ── IDE / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Documentation & meta ─────────────────────────────────────
docs/
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE

# ── Test / CI artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────
tests/
.coverage
coverage.json
htmlcov/
.github/

# ── Build scripts / misc ─────────────────────────────────────
build-install.sh
repo-to-prompt.codemod.js
requirements.txt
poetry.lock
Makefile
